today member states agreed to ratify the  Paris agreement as soon as possible and  we once again stress the importance for  member states to start taking the  necessary steps to finalize their  respective ratification procedures with  this council statement all Member States  recall the global political commitments  to fight climate change and make use of  the momentum of the historic outcome  that was reached in Paris with the  first-ever global and legally binding  climate agreement we need to have an  improved ETH system as of 2020 with the  right stimulus to lower carbon dioxide  emissions and therefore i'm happy to  mention that many member states  underlines the importance of flexibility  so that the EU can keep up with the  dynamic process we agreed upon in Paris  the council has welcomed the action plan  of the Commission for facilitating the  transition to a clear economy and the  council has expressed commitment to do  what needs to be done to achieve this  transition I start with wildlife  trafficking and here I very much welcome  that these conclusions are put forward  for adoption by des ministres only a few  months after the commission presented  the ambitious action plan on our fight  against wildlife trafficking the  Commission's proposal for a revamped  national emissions healing directive  aims at reducing the health impacts  through significant reductions in  cross-border air pollution across the  European Union member states at today's  environment Council there was broad  support for continuing negotiations with  a view to concluding before hopefully  the end of June
 

